  << java.util.StringJoiner over plain SLeeLa Strings: the joined elements,
     their count, the delimiter, prefix, suffix and the optional empty value.
     A null element is added as the text null, as Java does. length() is the
     UTF-16 length of toString(). merge(other) appends the elements of other
     (without its prefix and suffix) as one element, which gives the same text
     as Java. >>
